<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">All India Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1927">1927</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen, AIMIM, MIM</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen is a political party founded in Hyderabad State in 1927 to promote the interests of Muslims and the Nizam's rule. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qasim-razvi">Qasim Razvi</a> in 1946–1948 it opposed accession to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and organised the Razakar militia. Banned after the Indian annexation of 1948, it was revived in the late 1950s as the All India Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen and remains active in Hyderabad politics.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/all-india-majlis-e-ittehadul-muslimeen.jpg" alt="All India Majlis-e-Ittehadul Muslimeen" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VNC200 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:All_India_Majlis-e-Ittehadul_Muslimeen_logo.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
